  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city of Venice is built on more than 100 small islands in the marshy lagoon along the Adriatic Sea. Its unique position has made it vulnerable to flooding, especially during high tides and storms. In recent years, the city's authorities have been working on a new flood protection system. This system includes mobile barriers that can be raised to prevent water from entering the city. The barriers are designed to work in harmony with the existing sea walls and will help to protect the city from flooding.\n\nThe construction of the new flood protection system has sparked controversy among local residents. Some people are concerned about the impact on the city's historic architecture, while others believe that it is essential for preserving the city's cultural heritage. The authorities have promised to take into account the concerns of local residents and to ensure that the new system does not harm the city's unique character.\n\nVenice has been facing flooding problems for centuries. In fact, the city's famous St Mark's Square has flooded several times in recent years. However, the new flood protection system is expected to make a significant difference. The authorities are confident that it will help to protect the city from flooding and preserve its cultural heritage for future generations.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main reason why Venice's authorities have been working on a new flood protection system?\",\n      \"options\": [\"to improve the city's tourism industry\", \"to protect the city from flooding\", \"to preserve the city's historic architecture\", \"to reduce the city's carbon footprint\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is one of the concerns among local residents about the new flood protection system?\",\n      \"options\": [\"the impact on the city's economy\", \"the effect on the city's historic architecture\", \"the influence on the city's cultural heritage\", \"the cost of the project\"],\n      \"answer\": \"b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is meant by 'mobile barriers' in the context of the new flood protection system?\",\n      \"options\": [\"barriers that can be moved to different locations\", \"barriers that are made of mobile materials\", \"barriers that can be raised and lowered as needed\", \"barriers that are designed to work with the existing sea walls\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards the new flood protection system?\",\n      \"options\": [\"critical and opposed to it\", \"neutral and impartial\", \"supportive and positive\", \"skeptical but open-minded\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is one of the benefits that the new flood protection system is expected to bring?\",\n      \"options\": [\"a reduction in the city's carbon emissions\", \"an improvement in the city's tourism industry\", \"a preservation of the city's cultural heritage\", \"a decrease in the city's population\"],\n      \"answer\": \"c\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
